 "code_paths": {
  "1_transplant_spec_constructor": {
   "commit": "c7610ea19",
   "file": "archaeon/z80atlas/scheduler.py",
   "line": 255,
   "code": "t = json.loads(json.dumps(base)); t[\"transplant\"] = {\"from_run\": best[\"run_id\"], \"tapes\": tapes}; t[\"init\"] = \"random\""
  },
  "2a_transplant_branch_in_init": {
   "commit": "c7610ea19",
   "file": "archaeon/z80atlas/engine.py",
   "line": 153,
   "code": "transplant = spec.get(\"transplant\")                                   # late-stage lineage transport: tapes carried in the spec itself"
  },
  "2b_transplanted_tape_injection": {
   "commit": "c7610ea19",
   "file": "archaeon/z80atlas/engine.py",
   "line": 158,
   "code": "genomes[i] = bytes.fromhex(tapes[i])[:G].ljust(G, bytes(1))"
  },
  "3_spontaneous_predicate": {
   "commit": "c7610ea19",
   "file": "archaeon/z80atlas/engine.py",
   "line": 371,
   "code": "\"spontaneous_replication\": bool(spec[\"init\"] == \"random\" and phys in ENDO and births_endo >= F[\"spont_births\"] and last[\"pop\"] / N >= F[\"spont_pop_frac\"] and (last[\"fid\"] or 0) >= F[\"spont_fid\"]),"
  },
  "4_flag_and_weight": {
   "commit": "c7610ea19",
   "file": "archaeon/z80atlas/scheduler.py",
   "line": 101,
   "code": "if sig.get(\"spontaneous_replication\"): fl[\"spontaneous_replication\"] = 1"
  }
 },
 "why_false": "verify() builds each transplant spec from the source run's final population, puts those tapes in spec['transplant'] and sets init='random' (1). run() fills cells from spec['transplant']['tapes'] and never draws a random tape in that branch (2a/2b), so every founder is inserted material. The predicate tests only the nominal label spec['init']=='random' plus endogenous births, population and fidelity (3); it has no access to founder origin, so a transplanted lineage that keeps replicating satisfies it. The flag then scored +5 in the family table (4).",
